        programInfo: "The Child Tax Credit (CTC) is worth up to $2,200 per child under 17 for the 2025 tax year. It first reduces the taxes you owe — but most of it is nonrefundable, meaning if you owe little or no taxes, you don't get the full amount. The refundable portion (called the Additional Child Tax Credit, or ACTC) is capped at $1,700 per child and requires at least $2,500 in earned income. The Earned Income Tax Credit (EITC) is fully refundable — up to $8,046 for families with 3+ children, $7,152 for 2 children, or $4,328 for 1 child. Both credits require the filer (and spouse if filing jointly) to have a valid Social Security Number. Tax credits are not counted as income for programs like SNAP, Medicaid, or housing assistance.",
