              message: "Under the TCJA (2018\u20132025), Carlos and Elena could claim the Child Tax Credit for their three US-citizen children \u2014 about $" + ramirezCtcLost.toLocaleString() + "/year in refundable credits (the ACTC: 15% of earnings over $2,500, up to $1,700/child) that helped cover school supplies, clothing, and bills. When the OBBB was signed in July 2025, it required the filer to have an SSN, not just the children. Because Carlos and Elena file with ITINs, they were locked out entirely. They were never eligible for the EITC (which has always required filer SSNs), and now they\u2019ve lost the one tax credit their citizen children qualified them for." + ramirezCAMsg + " This loss is already reflected in your household\u2019s baseline stability score.",
